EAST BAY FOUNDERS WEEKLY
Friday, March 13, 2026

Hi all. What's happening for founders in Oakland, Berkeley, Emeryville and Alameda this week.

THIS WEEK AND NEXT
- Uptown coworking opens Monday March 16. Members' open house is Monday 5-7pm; come see the machine shop. The 20% discount applies to the first three months of any desk or office plan.
- Payroll tax session with a local CPA, Tuesday March 17, noon, online. Link in the portal. Forty signed up so far.
- Founder Breakfast, Friday March 20, 8:00am, Temescal. 25 max, 19 RSVPs. A reminder will go out Thursday.

NEWS
The SF-Oakland ferry moves to its spring schedule on March 23, which adds a 7:15am departure from the Ferry Building. Several of you asked. The last evening boat is still 8:40pm.

The city's small-business grant program opened its spring round: up to $25,000 for businesses under 25 employees that took a commercial lease in Oakland in the last year. Applications due April 15. Two members received grants last round.

The Pacific Plant Automation Expo member meetup happened Thursday; a dozen of us, and two members who had never met discovered they have the same customer. Small world, small region.

MEMBER NEWS
- A member's B2B payments company hired the sales lead posted here three weeks ago. The board works.
- A logistics-software member is running a customer advisory day in April and is looking for two more mid-size manufacturers to invite; reply if you can introduce one.

JOB BOARD: 15 open roles. https://eastbayfounders.org/jobs

Have a good weekend.

